WEBVTT

00:00:02.933 --> 00:00:04.744
Previously on Supernatural.

00:00:07.543 --> 00:00:11.101
Take your brother outside as
fast as you can! Now Dean! Go!

00:00:12.446 --> 00:00:14.024
Mary! No!

00:00:15.784 --> 00:00:16.923
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:18.048 --> 00:00:19.599
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:21.565 --> 00:00:22.964
I swore I was done hunting,

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.146
I can't do this alone.

00:00:30.785 --> 00:00:32.089
We got work to do.

00:00:32.459 --> 00:00:33.722
This is dad's single

00:00:33.763 --> 00:00:35.039
Most valuable possession.

00:00:35.066 --> 00:00:37.371
Everything he knows about
every evil thing is in here.

00:00:37.413 --> 00:00:39.380
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:39.421 --> 00:00:40.724
You know, saving people,

00:00:40.752 --> 00:00:41.836
Hunting things...

00:00:41.877 --> 00:00:42.755
Family business.

00:00:42.817 --> 00:00:43.283
No.

00:00:43.324 --> 00:00:44.696
I gotta find Jessica's killer.

00:00:44.737 --> 00:00:46.206
It's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.108
Sam, you know we're
gonna find dad, right?

00:00:49.917 --> 00:00:51.310
Yeah, I know.

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:07.740
Morning, daddy.

00:01:07.802 --> 00:01:09.179
Morning, sweetheart.

00:01:11.406 --> 00:01:13.674
All these workouts, Soph, I don't know.

00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:15.599
Guys don't like buff girls.

00:01:15.693 --> 00:01:18.561
Yeah, well, girls don't like
guys who still live at home.

00:01:25.465 --> 00:01:26.873
Be careful.

00:01:26.936 --> 00:01:28.031
I will.

00:03:04.337 --> 00:03:05.902
Can I get you anything else?

00:03:09.109 --> 00:03:10.674
Just the check, please.

00:03:10.772 --> 00:03:11.679
Okay.

00:03:16.452 --> 00:03:19.707
You know, Sam, we are allowed
to have fun once in a while.

00:03:22.538 --> 00:03:23.634
That's fun.

00:03:27.972 --> 00:03:29.990
Here, take a look at
this. I think I got one.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:31.930
Lake Manitoc, Wisconsin.

00:03:32.102 --> 00:03:33.729
Last week, Sophie Carlton,

00:03:33.828 --> 00:03:36.049
18, walks into the lake,

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.317
Doesn't walk out.

00:03:37.364 --> 00:03:39.038
Authorities dragged the water.

00:03:39.116 --> 00:03:40.008
Nothing.

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:43.048
Sophie Carlton is the third
Lake Manitoc drowning this year.

00:03:43.173 --> 00:03:44.941
None of the other
bodies were found, either

00:03:45.082 --> 00:03:46.224
They had a funeral two days ago.

00:03:46.286 --> 00:03:46.897
A funeral?

00:03:46.943 --> 00:03:48.977
Yes, they buried an empty coffin.

00:03:49.235 --> 00:03:52.114
For closure or whatever.

00:03:52.349 --> 00:03:53.428
Closure?

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:55.508
What closure?

00:03:55.712 --> 00:03:57.480
People don't just disappear, Dean.

00:03:57.714 --> 00:03:59.670
Other people just stop looking for them.

00:04:01.458 --> 00:04:02.553
Something you want to say to me?

00:04:02.589 --> 00:04:05.327
The trail for dad. It's getting colder.

00:04:05.452 --> 00:04:06.031
Every day.

00:04:06.062 --> 00:04:08.080
What are we supposed
to do? I don't know.

00:04:08.299 --> 00:04:09.128
Something.

00:04:09.269 --> 00:04:10.411
Anything. No one.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:11.840
I'm sick of this attitude.

00:04:12.168 --> 00:04:13.749
You don't think I want to
find dad as much as you do?

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:14.562
Yeah, I know you do it.

00:04:14.593 --> 00:04:17.269
I'm the one that's been with him every
single day for the past two years.

00:04:17.378 --> 00:04:19.569
While you've been off to
college going to pep rallies.

00:04:19.709 --> 00:04:20.898
We will find dad,

00:04:20.961 --> 00:04:23.167
But until then, we're
gonna kill everything bad,

00:04:23.307 --> 00:04:24.841
Between here and there.

00:04:25.654 --> 00:04:26.703
Okay?

00:04:33.361 --> 00:04:35.332
All right, Lake Manitoc.

00:04:36.036 --> 00:04:36.411
Hey.

00:04:36.521 --> 00:04:36.959
Huh?

00:04:37.006 --> 00:04:37.804
How far?

00:04:59.103 --> 00:04:59.963
Will Carlton?

00:05:00.339 --> 00:05:01.027
Yeah, that's right.

00:05:01.183 --> 00:05:02.247
I'm agent Ford.

00:05:02.428 --> 00:05:03.773
This is agent Hamill.

00:05:04.258 --> 00:05:06.042
We're with the U.S. Wildlife service.

00:05:13.344 --> 00:05:15.221
She was about 100 yards out.

00:05:16.848 --> 00:05:17.943
That's where she got dragged down.

00:05:18.006 --> 00:05:19.351
And you're sure she didn't just drown?

00:05:19.383 --> 00:05:19.821
Yeah.

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:21.573
She was a varsity swimmer.

00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:23.450
She practically grew up in that lake.

00:05:24.576 --> 00:05:26.751
She's as safe out there
as in her own bathtub.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:28.597
So no splashing,

00:05:28.691 --> 00:05:29.802
No signs of distress?

00:05:29.849 --> 00:05:31.006
No, that's what I'm telling you.

00:05:31.183 --> 00:05:33.326
Did you see any shadows in the water,

00:05:34.171 --> 00:05:35.016
Maybe,

00:05:35.219 --> 00:05:37.659
Some dark shape breach the surface?

00:05:37.706 --> 00:05:39.724
No, again, she was really far out there.

00:05:39.818 --> 00:05:41.570
You ever see any strange
tracks by the shoreline?

00:05:41.601 --> 00:05:42.509
No, never.

00:05:42.618 --> 00:05:43.432
Why?

00:05:43.557 --> 00:05:44.903
What do you think's out there?

00:05:45.357 --> 00:05:47.641
We'll let you know as soon as we do.

00:05:49.878 --> 00:05:51.380
What about your father?

00:05:51.615 --> 00:05:53.070
Can we talk to him?

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:55.782
Look.

00:05:55.891 --> 00:05:57.377
If you don't mind, I mean,

00:05:57.581 --> 00:06:00.100
He didn't see anything, and
he's kind of been through a lot.

00:06:00.991 --> 00:06:02.243
We understand.

00:06:08.598 --> 00:06:09.542
Now, I'm sorry, but,

00:06:09.568 --> 00:06:13.767
Why does the wildlife service
care about an accidental drowning?

00:06:13.902 --> 00:06:15.247
You sure it's accidental?

00:06:15.503 --> 00:06:17.489
Will Carlton saw
something grab his sister.

00:06:18.053 --> 00:06:19.195
Like what?

00:06:19.633 --> 00:06:20.665
Here, sit, please.

00:06:20.712 --> 00:06:23.748
There are no indigenous
carnivores in that lake.

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:26.642
There's nothing even big
enough to pull down a person,

00:06:26.728 --> 00:06:28.574
Unless it was the Loch Ness monster.

00:06:29.427 --> 00:06:30.882
Yeah, right.

00:06:31.007 --> 00:06:35.075
Will Carlton was traumatized, and
sometimes the mind plays tricks.

00:06:35.502 --> 00:06:36.362
Still,

00:06:36.894 --> 00:06:40.461
We dragged that entire lake.
We even ran a sonar sweep,

00:06:40.889 --> 00:06:43.282
Just to be sure, and there
was nothing down there.

00:06:43.361 --> 00:06:45.410
That's weird, though.

00:06:45.817 --> 00:06:47.444
That's the third missing body this year.

00:06:47.527 --> 00:06:48.622
I know.

00:06:49.279 --> 00:06:51.063
These are people from my town.

00:06:51.251 --> 00:06:52.721
These are people I care about.

00:06:52.815 --> 00:06:53.644
I know.

00:06:55.026 --> 00:06:56.074
Anyway . . .

00:06:57.780 --> 00:06:59.031
All this.

00:07:00.361 --> 00:07:02.239
It won't be a problem much longer.

00:07:02.817 --> 00:07:03.866
What do you mean?

00:07:04.654 --> 00:07:06.188
Well, the dam, of course.

00:07:07.502 --> 00:07:08.691
Of course.

00:07:08.957 --> 00:07:09.864
The dam.

00:07:10.177 --> 00:07:11.210
It's, uh...

00:07:12.649 --> 00:07:13.494
It sprung a leak.

00:07:13.572 --> 00:07:14.699
It's falling apart,

00:07:15.309 --> 00:07:18.067
And the feds won't give
us the grant to repair it,

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:19.820
So they've opened the spillway.

00:07:20.445 --> 00:07:22.229
In another six months,

00:07:22.839 --> 00:07:24.263
There won't be much of a lake.

00:07:24.513 --> 00:07:26.082
There won't be much of a town, either,

00:07:26.223 --> 00:07:27.287
But as federal wildlife,

00:07:27.412 --> 00:07:28.805
You already knew that.

00:07:29.509 --> 00:07:30.338
Exactly.

00:07:30.995 --> 00:07:32.935
Sorry, am I interrupting?

00:07:33.472 --> 00:07:34.692
I think come back later.

00:07:34.833 --> 00:07:36.835
Gentlemen, this is my daughter.

00:07:37.258 --> 00:07:38.447
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:07:38.791 --> 00:07:39.714
I'm Dean.

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:41.482
Andrea Bar. Hi.

00:07:41.686 --> 00:07:42.108
Hi.

00:07:42.332 --> 00:07:43.849
They're from the wildlife service,

00:07:44.459 --> 00:07:45.711
About the lake.

00:07:49.878 --> 00:07:51.208
Oh, hey, there.

00:07:51.494 --> 00:07:52.448
What's your name?

00:07:58.769 --> 00:08:00.099
His name is Lucas.

00:08:02.974 --> 00:08:03.850
Is he okay?

00:08:03.928 --> 00:08:05.555
My grandson's been through a lot.

00:08:06.478 --> 00:08:07.793
We all have.

00:08:08.669 --> 00:08:09.482
Well,

00:08:10.254 --> 00:08:11.818
If there's anything
else I can do for you,

00:08:11.835 --> 00:08:12.899
Please, let me know.

00:08:13.023 --> 00:08:13.774
Thanks.

00:08:14.655 --> 00:08:16.360
You know, now that you mentioned it,

00:08:16.454 --> 00:08:19.693
Could you point us in the direction
of a reasonably priced motel?

00:08:19.885 --> 00:08:22.592
Lake front motel, go around
the corner, it's two blocks up.

00:08:22.655 --> 00:08:23.374
Two.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:25.001
Would you mind showing us?

00:08:26.394 --> 00:08:28.068
You want me to walk you two blocks?

00:08:28.146 --> 00:08:29.429
Not if it's any trouble.

00:08:30.038 --> 00:08:31.900
I'm headed that way anyway.

00:08:33.042 --> 00:08:35.092
I'll be back to pick up lucas at 3:00.

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:36.922
We'll go to the park, okay, sweetie?

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:41.981
Thanks again.

00:08:43.045 --> 00:08:44.265
So, cute kid.

00:08:44.625 --> 00:08:45.204
Thanks.

00:08:47.353 --> 00:08:48.824
Kids are the best, huh?

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:53.960
There it is.

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:56.072
Like I said, two blocks.

00:08:56.150 --> 00:08:56.917
Thanks.

00:08:57.730 --> 00:09:00.171
Must be hard with your
sense of direction,

00:09:00.547 --> 00:09:03.441
Never being able to find your
way to a decent pickup line.

00:09:04.979 --> 00:09:06.215
Enjoy your stay.

00:09:08.077 --> 00:09:09.204
"Kids are the best"?

00:09:09.803 --> 00:09:11.649
You don't even like kids. I love kids.

00:09:11.712 --> 00:09:13.949
Name three children that you even know.

00:09:20.676 --> 00:09:21.740
I'm thinking.

00:09:22.147 --> 00:09:24.650
So there's the three
drowning victims this year.

00:09:24.681 --> 00:09:25.620
And before that?

00:09:25.761 --> 00:09:28.530
Yeah, six more,

00:09:28.561 --> 00:09:30.141
Spread outover the past 35 years.

00:09:30.282 --> 00:09:32.081
Those bodies were
never recovered, either.

00:09:32.691 --> 00:09:34.178
If there is something out there,

00:09:34.328 --> 00:09:35.283
It's picking up its pace.

00:09:35.345 --> 00:09:36.863
So we got a lake monster on a binge?

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:39.601
This whole lake monster
theory, it just bugs me.

00:09:39.867 --> 00:09:40.712
Why?

00:09:41.249 --> 00:09:43.001
Loch Ness, lake Champlain

00:09:43.032 --> 00:09:45.598
There are literally hundreds
of eyewitness accounts,

00:09:45.645 --> 00:09:47.507
But here, almost nothing.

00:09:47.835 --> 00:09:49.115
Whatever it is out there,

00:09:49.416 --> 00:09:50.777
Noone's living to talk about it.

00:09:51.028 --> 00:09:52.295
Wait, Bar,

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:54.428
Christopher Bar, where have
I heard that name before?

00:09:54.459 --> 00:09:57.072
Christopher Bar, the victim in may.

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:00.639
Christopher Bar was Andrea's husband,

00:10:00.934 --> 00:10:02.373
Lucas' father.

00:10:02.831 --> 00:10:03.708
Apparently,

00:10:03.942 --> 00:10:05.773
He took Lucas out swimming.

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:09.246
Lucas was on a floating wooden
platform when Chris drowned,

00:10:09.543 --> 00:10:10.685
Two hours,

00:10:11.124 --> 00:10:12.970
Before the kid got rescued.

00:10:16.677 --> 00:10:18.711
Maybe we have an eyewitness after all.

00:10:19.196 --> 00:10:21.011
No wonder that kid was so freaked out.

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:24.958
Watching one of your parents die
isn't something you just get over.

00:10:27.133 --> 00:10:28.385
Can we join you?

00:10:32.377 --> 00:10:33.801
I'm here with my son.

00:10:37.196 --> 00:10:38.432
Mind if I say hi?

00:10:40.786 --> 00:10:44.212
Tell your friend this whole "jerry
maguire" thing's not gonna work on me.

00:10:45.026 --> 00:10:46.700
I don't think that's what this is about.

00:10:49.991 --> 00:10:51.133
How's it going?

00:10:58.730 --> 00:11:00.826
Oh, I used to love these things.

00:11:07.495 --> 00:11:09.451
So crayons is more your thing?

00:11:09.983 --> 00:11:11.970
That's cool. Chicks dig artists.

00:11:14.425 --> 00:11:15.786
Hey, these are pretty good.

00:11:17.366 --> 00:11:19.431
You mind if I sit and
draw with you for a while?

00:11:19.874 --> 00:11:21.454
I'm not so bad myself.

00:11:30.964 --> 00:11:32.826
You know, I'm thinking you can hear me.

00:11:33.373 --> 00:11:34.797
You just don't want to talk.

00:11:35.345 --> 00:11:37.535
I don't know exactly
what happened to your dad,

00:11:38.637 --> 00:11:40.501
But I know it was something real bad.

00:11:44.005 --> 00:11:45.585
I think I know how you feel.

00:11:48.041 --> 00:11:50.325
When I was your age, I saw something.

00:11:57.208 --> 00:11:58.397
Anyway . . .

00:12:00.404 --> 00:12:03.221
Maybe you don't think
anyone will listen to you.

00:12:03.961 --> 00:12:04.947
Or, uh...

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:07.963
Or believe you.

00:12:08.573 --> 00:12:10.341
I want you to know that I will.

00:12:11.749 --> 00:12:13.266
You don't even have to

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:15.331
Say anything. You
could draw me a picture,

00:12:15.394 --> 00:12:16.740
About what you saw that day,

00:12:17.038 --> 00:12:18.274
With your dad,

00:12:19.572 --> 00:12:20.433
On the lake.

00:12:24.517 --> 00:12:25.425
Okay,

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:26.535
No problem.

00:12:27.005 --> 00:12:28.022
This is for you.

00:12:29.148 --> 00:12:30.462
This is my family.

00:12:31.761 --> 00:12:32.997
That's my dad.

00:12:33.362 --> 00:12:34.206
That's...

00:12:35.912 --> 00:12:36.944
That's my mom.

00:12:37.715 --> 00:12:39.311
That's my geek brother,

00:12:40.203 --> 00:12:41.392
And that's me.

00:12:45.288 --> 00:12:46.977
All right, so I'm a sucky artist.

00:12:47.404 --> 00:12:48.765
I'll see you around, Lucas.

00:13:01.971 --> 00:13:04.912
Lucas hasn't said a
word, not even to me,

00:13:05.527 --> 00:13:06.623
Not since

00:13:07.577 --> 00:13:09.157
His dad's accident.

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:10.972
Yeah, we heard.

00:13:11.254 --> 00:13:12.177
Sorry.

00:13:13.303 --> 00:13:15.102
What are the doctors saying?

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:17.879
That it's a kind of
post-Traumatic stress.

00:13:17.973 --> 00:13:19.194
That can't be easy

00:13:19.350 --> 00:13:20.054
For either of you.

00:13:20.117 --> 00:13:21.619
We moved in with my dad.

00:13:22.589 --> 00:13:24.247
He helps out a lot.

00:13:26.242 --> 00:13:27.384
It's just...

00:13:28.964 --> 00:13:32.312
When I think about what Lucas
went through, what he saw...

00:13:34.659 --> 00:13:35.926
Kids are strong.

00:13:36.486 --> 00:13:38.504
You'd be surprised
what they can deal with.

00:13:39.302 --> 00:13:40.366
You know,

00:13:40.883 --> 00:13:42.494
He used to have such life.

00:13:42.776 --> 00:13:45.169
He was hard to keep up
with, to tell you the truth.

00:13:46.369 --> 00:13:47.761
Now he just sits there,

00:13:47.871 --> 00:13:50.483
Drawing those pictures,
playing with those army men.

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:52.022
I just wish.

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:53.805
Hey, sweetie.

00:13:59.318 --> 00:14:00.100
Thanks.

00:14:01.132 --> 00:14:02.259
Thanks, Lucas.

00:14:20.375 --> 00:14:21.627
Hey, dad.

00:14:23.019 --> 00:14:24.834
You should probably eat something.

00:14:26.982 --> 00:14:28.547
I'm gonna make some dinner, okay?

00:16:23.125 --> 00:16:24.189
So,

00:16:24.299 --> 00:16:26.317
I think it's safe to say
we can rule out Nessie.

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:27.146
What do you mean?

00:16:27.229 --> 00:16:30.358
I just drove past the Carlton
house. There was an ambulance there.

00:16:30.561 --> 00:16:31.907
Will Carlton is dead.

00:16:32.141 --> 00:16:32.720
He drowned?

00:16:32.767 --> 00:16:34.379
Yep, in the sink.

00:16:35.098 --> 00:16:36.240
What the hell?

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:38.858
So this isn't a creature. We're
dealing with something else.

00:16:38.905 --> 00:16:39.687
Yeah, but what?

00:16:39.734 --> 00:16:40.344
I don't know.

00:16:40.469 --> 00:16:41.611
A water wraith maybe?

00:16:41.846 --> 00:16:42.925
Some kind of demon?

00:16:43.137 --> 00:16:44.811
I mean, something that controls water

00:16:47.242 --> 00:16:48.791
water that comes from the Same source.

00:16:48.854 --> 00:16:49.667
The lake Yeah

00:16:49.699 --> 00:16:51.607
Which would explain why
it's upping the body count.

00:16:51.983 --> 00:16:54.877
The lake is draining. It'll be dry in
a few months. Whatever this thing is,

00:16:54.949 --> 00:16:56.388
Whatever it wants,

00:16:56.717 --> 00:16:57.577
It's running out of time.

00:16:57.609 --> 00:16:59.158
And if it can get through the pipes,

00:16:59.596 --> 00:17:00.602
It can get to anyone,

00:17:00.665 --> 00:17:01.603
Almost anywhere.

00:17:01.697 --> 00:17:03.700
This is gonna happen again soon.

00:17:03.981 --> 00:17:05.483
And we do know one other thing for sure.

00:17:05.515 --> 00:17:07.815
We know this has got something
to do with Bill Carlton.

00:17:07.877 --> 00:17:08.901
It took both his kids.

00:17:08.948 --> 00:17:10.199
And I've been asking around.

00:17:10.324 --> 00:17:11.560
Lucas' dad, Chris

00:17:12.045 --> 00:17:13.328
Bill Carlton's godson.

00:17:14.001 --> 00:17:15.753
Let's go pay Mr. Carlton a visit.

00:17:18.265 --> 00:17:19.532
Mr. Carlton?

00:17:22.254 --> 00:17:24.272
We'd like to ask you a few questions,

00:17:24.351 --> 00:17:25.039
If you don't mind.

00:17:25.102 --> 00:17:27.495
We're from the department I
don't care who you're with.

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:30.614
I've answered enough questions today.

00:17:32.694 --> 00:17:35.432
Your son said he saw
something in that lake.

00:17:36.402 --> 00:17:37.560
What about you?

00:17:38.098 --> 00:17:39.663
You ever see anything out there?

00:17:41.149 --> 00:17:42.119
Mr. Carlton,

00:17:42.150 --> 00:17:44.106
Sophie's drowning and Will's death.

00:17:44.403 --> 00:17:45.874
We think there might be a connection,

00:17:45.968 --> 00:17:48.862
To you or your family.
My children are gone.

00:17:52.447 --> 00:17:53.214
It's...

00:17:56.358 --> 00:17:58.032
It's worse than dying.

00:18:05.285 --> 00:18:06.318
Go away...

00:18:07.976 --> 00:18:08.852
Please.

00:18:11.845 --> 00:18:13.081
What do you think?

00:18:14.051 --> 00:18:16.053
I think the poor guy's
been through hell.

00:18:16.836 --> 00:18:18.650
I also think he's not
telling us something.

00:18:18.682 --> 00:18:19.699
So now what?

00:18:22.499 --> 00:18:23.406
What is it?

00:18:27.114 --> 00:18:29.727
Maybe Bill's not the only
one who knows something.

00:18:40.454 --> 00:18:42.237
I'm sorry, but I don't
think it's a good idea.

00:18:42.337 --> 00:18:43.432
I just need to talk to him,

00:18:43.495 --> 00:18:44.559
Just for a few minutes.

00:18:44.731 --> 00:18:46.342
He won't say anything.

00:18:46.827 --> 00:18:48.454
What good's it gonna do? Andrea,

00:18:48.658 --> 00:18:50.269
We think more people might get hurt.

00:18:51.807 --> 00:18:53.215
We think something's
happening out there.

00:18:53.324 --> 00:18:55.953
My husband, the others,
they just drowned.

00:18:56.375 --> 00:18:57.095
That's all.

00:18:57.142 --> 00:18:58.300
If that's what you really believe,

00:18:58.362 --> 00:18:59.129
Then we'll go,

00:18:59.415 --> 00:19:01.386
But if you think there's
even a possibility

00:19:01.699 --> 00:19:03.483
That something else
could be going on here,

00:19:05.079 --> 00:19:06.549
Please let me talk to your son.

00:19:21.968 --> 00:19:23.251
Hey, Lucas.

00:19:24.773 --> 00:19:25.900
You remember me?

00:19:35.156 --> 00:19:36.705
You know, I, uh...

00:19:38.473 --> 00:19:40.773
I wanted to thank you
for that last drawing

00:19:43.928 --> 00:19:45.586
but the thing is

00:19:46.071 --> 00:19:47.448
I need your help again.

00:20:00.418 --> 00:20:02.061
How did you know to draw this?

00:20:05.038 --> 00:20:07.150
Did you know something
bad was gonna happen?

00:20:09.247 --> 00:20:10.295
Maybe you could

00:20:10.717 --> 00:20:12.250
Nod yes or no

00:20:12.344 --> 00:20:13.173
For me.

00:20:15.645 --> 00:20:16.693
You're scared.

00:20:21.869 --> 00:20:22.730
It's okay.

00:20:23.559 --> 00:20:24.732
I understand.

00:20:25.249 --> 00:20:26.610
See, when I was your age,

00:20:26.688 --> 00:20:29.176
I saw something real
bad happen to my mom,

00:20:31.934 --> 00:20:33.326
And I was scared, too.

00:20:36.116 --> 00:20:37.524
I didn't feel like talking,

00:20:37.915 --> 00:20:39.057
Just like you,

00:20:40.246 --> 00:20:41.795
But, see, my mom,

00:20:44.204 --> 00:20:46.269
I know she wanted me to be brave.

00:20:49.591 --> 00:20:51.249
I think about that every day.

00:20:56.431 --> 00:20:58.418
And I do my best to be brave.

00:21:02.397 --> 00:21:04.003
And maybe your dad

00:21:06.111 --> 00:21:07.707
Wants you to be brave, too.

00:21:29.668 --> 00:21:30.826
Thanks, Lucas.

00:21:35.696 --> 00:21:38.136
Andrea said the kid never drew
like that till his dad died.

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:41.547
There are cases going
through a traumatic experience

00:21:41.735 --> 00:21:46.386
Could make certain people more sensitive
to premonitions, psychic tendencies.

00:21:46.397 --> 00:21:48.767
What if Lucas is
tapping into it somehow?

00:21:49.059 --> 00:21:51.030
It's only a matter of time
before somebody else drowns,

00:21:51.044 --> 00:21:52.702
So if you got a better lead, please.

00:21:53.458 --> 00:21:54.460
All right.

00:21:54.699 --> 00:21:55.654
We got another house to find.

00:21:55.670 --> 00:21:59.096
There's about a thousand yellow
two-Stories in this county alone.

00:21:59.722 --> 00:22:00.927
See this church?

00:22:01.381 --> 00:22:03.415
I bet there's less than a
thousand of those around here.

00:22:04.218 --> 00:22:07.002
Oh, college boy thinks he's so smart.

00:22:14.363 --> 00:22:15.709
You know, um...

00:22:17.570 --> 00:22:18.947
What you said about mom.

00:22:21.951 --> 00:22:23.703
You never told me that before.

00:22:24.251 --> 00:22:25.503
It's no big deal.

00:22:29.669 --> 00:22:32.219
Oh, god, we're not gonna have
to hug or anything, are we?

00:22:58.620 --> 00:23:00.263
We're sorry to bother you, ma'am,

00:23:00.325 --> 00:23:02.735
But does a little boy
live here by chance?

00:23:02.876 --> 00:23:03.877
He might wear

00:23:04.002 --> 00:23:05.082
A blue ball cap,

00:23:05.348 --> 00:23:06.709
Has a red bicycle.

00:23:07.578 --> 00:23:08.626
No, sir.

00:23:10.081 --> 00:23:12.349
Not for a very long time.

00:23:13.898 --> 00:23:16.652
Peter's been gone 35 years now.

00:23:19.591 --> 00:23:21.297
The police never

00:23:22.454 --> 00:23:25.255
I never had any idea what happened.

00:23:28.464 --> 00:23:30.483
He just disappeared.

00:23:31.161 --> 00:23:32.522
Losing him,

00:23:34.697 --> 00:23:35.635
You know,

00:23:37.129 --> 00:23:37.708
It's...

00:23:39.841 --> 00:23:41.702
It's worse than dying.

00:23:46.729 --> 00:23:48.482
Did he disappear from here,

00:23:48.544 --> 00:23:49.530
I mean, from this house?

00:23:49.608 --> 00:23:50.813
He was supposed to

00:23:51.658 --> 00:23:52.784
Ride his bike

00:23:53.050 --> 00:23:54.208
Straight home

00:23:54.302 --> 00:23:55.412
After school,

00:23:55.835 --> 00:23:57.352
And he never showed up.

00:24:14.326 --> 00:24:16.250
"Peter Sweeney and Billy Carlton,

00:24:16.521 --> 00:24:17.976
1970."

00:24:23.723 --> 00:24:25.053
You've taken everything,

00:24:27.572 --> 00:24:28.824
Everyone.

00:24:31.785 --> 00:24:33.084
I've got nothing left.

00:24:36.541 --> 00:24:38.012
I didn't understand.

00:24:40.191 --> 00:24:41.490
I didn't believe.

00:24:44.353 --> 00:24:45.698
Now I think I do.

00:24:48.098 --> 00:24:50.147
I think I finally know what you want.

00:24:55.221 --> 00:24:57.427
Okay, this little boy,
Peter Sweeney, vanishes,

00:24:57.474 --> 00:24:59.820
And this is all connected
to Bill Carlton somehow.

00:24:59.852 --> 00:25:01.776
Bill sure as hell seems
to be hiding something.

00:25:01.839 --> 00:25:03.262
And Bill, the people he loves

00:25:03.408 --> 00:25:04.253
They're all getting punished.

00:25:04.457 --> 00:25:05.865
So that Bill did something to Peter.

00:25:06.084 --> 00:25:07.210
What if Bill killed him?

00:25:07.711 --> 00:25:09.056
Peter's spirit would be furious.

00:25:09.135 --> 00:25:10.574
It'd want revenge. It's possible.

00:25:15.988 --> 00:25:17.537
Mr. Carlton!

00:25:20.666 --> 00:25:22.089
Hey. Check it out.

00:25:29.989 --> 00:25:32.148
Mr. Carlton! You need to come back!

00:25:33.353 --> 00:25:35.559
Come out of the water !
Turn the boat around!

00:25:49.364 --> 00:25:50.881
Baby, what's wrong?

00:25:54.011 --> 00:25:55.575
Sam, Dean.

00:25:56.394 --> 00:25:58.287
I didn't expect to see you here.

00:25:59.273 --> 00:26:01.181
So now you're on a first-Name basis.

00:26:02.308 --> 00:26:03.450
What are you doing here?

00:26:03.502 --> 00:26:04.706
I brought you dinner.

00:26:05.051 --> 00:26:07.961
I'm sorry, sweetheart. I
don't really have the time.

00:26:12.081 --> 00:26:13.786
I heard about Bill Carlton.

00:26:14.083 --> 00:26:16.446
Is it true? Is something
going on with the lake?

00:26:18.417 --> 00:26:20.185
Right now, we don't
know what the truth is,

00:26:20.451 --> 00:26:22.939
But I think it might be better
if you and lucas went on home.

00:26:25.874 --> 00:26:27.595
Lucas, hey, what is it?

00:26:27.845 --> 00:26:29.238
Lucas. Lucas.

00:26:29.488 --> 00:26:31.882
Lucas, it's okay. It's okay. Hey,

00:26:31.960 --> 00:26:34.404
Lucas, it's okay. It's okay.

00:26:56.856 --> 00:26:59.985
Okay, just so I'm clear, you see . . .

00:27:00.219 --> 00:27:01.142
Something

00:27:01.627 --> 00:27:03.161
Attack Bill's boat,

00:27:03.630 --> 00:27:04.835
Sending Bill,

00:27:06.238 --> 00:27:08.647
Who is a very good swimmer, by the way,

00:27:08.913 --> 00:27:10.196
Into the drink,

00:27:11.025 --> 00:27:12.746
And you never see him again?

00:27:15.107 --> 00:27:16.640
Yeah, that about sums it up.

00:27:16.687 --> 00:27:18.189
And I'm supposed to believe this,

00:27:18.236 --> 00:27:20.958
Even though I've already
sonar-Swept that entire lake

00:27:21.381 --> 00:27:23.665
And what you're describing is impossible

00:27:24.353 --> 00:27:26.652
And you're not really wildlife service?

00:27:27.939 --> 00:27:28.768
That's right,

00:27:29.018 --> 00:27:29.722
I checked.

00:27:30.004 --> 00:27:31.631
The department's never heard of you two.

00:27:32.137 --> 00:27:32.841
See?

00:27:32.935 --> 00:27:34.843
Now, we can explain that. Enough,

00:27:35.594 --> 00:27:36.674
Please.

00:27:37.816 --> 00:27:40.194
The only reason you're
breathing free air

00:27:40.449 --> 00:27:44.298
Is one of Bill's neighbors saw him
steering out that boat just before you did.

00:27:45.033 --> 00:27:45.691
So

00:27:45.925 --> 00:27:47.505
We have a couple of options here.

00:27:47.803 --> 00:27:49.988
I can arrest you for
impersonating government officials

00:27:50.004 --> 00:27:53.608
And hold you as material witnesses
to Bill Carlton's disappearance,

00:27:53.857 --> 00:27:54.670
Or

00:27:54.983 --> 00:27:57.799
We can chalk this all up to a bad day,

00:27:58.070 --> 00:27:59.525
You get into your car,

00:27:59.665 --> 00:28:02.548
You put this town in
your rearview mirror,

00:28:02.561 --> 00:28:05.704
And you don't ever darken my doorstep

00:28:05.762 --> 00:28:06.476
Again!

00:28:09.182 --> 00:28:10.746
Door number two sounds good.

00:28:10.997 --> 00:28:12.499
That's the one I'd pick.

00:28:27.428 --> 00:28:28.429
Baby...

00:28:30.267 --> 00:28:31.800
What are you doing up?

00:28:34.617 --> 00:28:36.353
Come on, let's go to bed.

00:28:57.668 --> 00:28:58.669
Green.

00:28:58.810 --> 00:28:59.498
What?

00:28:59.623 --> 00:29:01.016
Light's green.

00:29:08.295 --> 00:29:10.126
Ah, the interstate's the other way.

00:29:10.157 --> 00:29:10.767
I know.

00:29:35.056 --> 00:29:37.481
But, Dean, this job, I think it's over.

00:29:37.528 --> 00:29:38.372
I'm not so sure.

00:29:38.419 --> 00:29:41.439
If bill murdered Peter Sweeney
and Peter's spirit got its revenge,

00:29:41.595 --> 00:29:43.692
Case closed. The spirit
should be at rest.

00:29:43.737 --> 00:29:46.053
All right, so what if we take
off and this thing isn't done?

00:29:46.350 --> 00:29:48.374
What if we missed something?
What if more people get hurt?

00:29:48.452 --> 00:29:50.032
But why would you think that?

00:29:51.846 --> 00:29:53.520
Because Lucas was really scared.

00:29:53.786 --> 00:29:55.273
That's what this is about?

00:29:56.243 --> 00:29:58.574
I just don't want to leave
town till I know the kid's okay.

00:29:59.043 --> 00:30:00.029
Who are you,

00:30:00.138 --> 00:30:01.969
And what have you done with my brother?

00:30:04.346 --> 00:30:05.551
Shut up.

00:31:35.888 --> 00:31:37.343
Are you sure about this?

00:31:37.671 --> 00:31:38.970
It's pretty late, man.

00:31:42.291 --> 00:31:43.762
Lucas? Lucas!

00:31:46.703 --> 00:31:47.626
Lucas!

00:32:26.697 --> 00:32:27.761
Can you tell me?

00:32:29.893 --> 00:32:30.754
No

00:32:38.798 --> 00:32:40.503
It doesn't make any sense.

00:32:44.602 --> 00:32:46.135
I'm going crazy.

00:32:47.152 --> 00:32:48.671
No, you're not.

00:32:50.095 --> 00:32:51.269
Tell me what happened.

00:32:51.879 --> 00:32:52.818
Everything.

00:32:57.008 --> 00:32:58.134
I heard...

00:33:01.107 --> 00:33:02.844
I thought I heard...

00:33:05.152 --> 00:33:06.967
There was this voice.

00:33:07.483 --> 00:33:08.453
What did it say?

00:33:08.500 --> 00:33:09.345
It said

00:33:10.305 --> 00:33:12.558
It said, "come play with me."

00:33:20.550 --> 00:33:22.052
What's happening?

00:33:41.342 --> 00:33:43.157
Do you recognize the
kids in these pictures?

00:33:43.282 --> 00:33:44.033
What?

00:33:45.942 --> 00:33:46.834
No, I huh...

00:33:46.912 --> 00:33:50.025
I mean, except that's
my dad right there.

00:33:50.233 --> 00:33:51.594
He must have been about

00:33:52.204 --> 00:33:53.831
12 in these pictures.

00:33:55.460 --> 00:33:56.821
Chris Bar's drowning

00:33:57.102 --> 00:33:59.465
The connection wasn't to Bill
Carlton. It must have been to sheriff.

00:33:59.527 --> 00:34:00.982
Bill and the sheriff,

00:34:01.342 --> 00:34:02.954
They were both involved with Peter.

00:34:03.225 --> 00:34:04.252
What about Chris?

00:34:04.867 --> 00:34:07.026
My dad, what are you talking about?

00:34:07.261 --> 00:34:08.153
Lucas?

00:34:08.873 --> 00:34:10.202
Lucas, what is it?

00:34:16.509 --> 00:34:18.684
Lucas, honey?

00:34:30.441 --> 00:34:32.881
You and Lucas get back to the
house and stay there, okay?

00:34:57.183 --> 00:34:58.435
Peter's bike.

00:34:59.233 --> 00:35:00.281
Who are you?

00:35:03.676 --> 00:35:05.162
Put the gun down, Jake.

00:35:05.866 --> 00:35:07.341
How did you know that was there?

00:35:07.388 --> 00:35:08.233
What happened?

00:35:08.437 --> 00:35:09.985
You and Bill killed Peter,

00:35:10.330 --> 00:35:12.176
Drowned him in the lake,
and then buried the bike?

00:35:13.130 --> 00:35:14.851
You can't bury the truth, Jake.

00:35:16.030 --> 00:35:17.657
Nothing stays buried.

00:35:21.224 --> 00:35:22.726
Go to your room, sweetie.

00:35:24.009 --> 00:35:24.854
Now.

00:35:24.901 --> 00:35:27.172
Lock the door and wait
for me. Don't come out.

00:35:27.546 --> 00:35:28.907
I don't know what the
hell you're talking about.

00:35:28.929 --> 00:35:31.348
You and Bill killed Peter
Sweeney 35 years ago.

00:35:31.442 --> 00:35:32.360
That's what the hell I'm talking about.

00:35:32.365 --> 00:35:32.975
Dad

00:35:33.256 --> 00:35:35.337
And now you got one
seriously pissed-Off spirit.

00:35:35.384 --> 00:35:36.636
It's gonna take Andrea,

00:35:36.745 --> 00:35:37.527
Lucas,

00:35:37.827 --> 00:35:38.812
Everyone you love.

00:35:39.313 --> 00:35:40.393
It's gonna drown them,

00:35:40.799 --> 00:35:42.661
And it's gonna drag their
bodies god knows where.

00:35:42.958 --> 00:35:45.227
So you can feel the Same
pain Peter's mom felt.

00:35:46.088 --> 00:35:47.386
And then after that,

00:35:48.276 --> 00:35:49.325
It's gonna take you,

00:35:49.638 --> 00:35:51.359
And it's not gonna stop until it does.

00:35:52.250 --> 00:35:53.314
How do you know that?

00:35:53.424 --> 00:35:55.880
Because that's exactly
what it did to Bill Carlton.

00:35:55.927 --> 00:35:57.072
Listen to yourselves,

00:35:57.323 --> 00:35:57.933
Both of you.

00:35:57.995 --> 00:35:59.122
You're insane.

00:35:59.169 --> 00:36:01.359
I don't really give a rat's
ass what you think of us,

00:36:02.367 --> 00:36:04.010
But if we're gonna
bring down this spirit,

00:36:04.229 --> 00:36:05.778
We need to find the remains,

00:36:06.044 --> 00:36:06.857
Salt them,

00:36:06.998 --> 00:36:08.125
And burn them into dust.

00:36:08.328 --> 00:36:09.840
Tell me you buried Peter somewhere.

00:36:09.862 --> 00:36:11.593
Tell me you didn't just
let him go in the lake.

00:36:16.960 --> 00:36:19.651
Come play with me.

00:36:23.520 --> 00:36:24.083
Dad,

00:36:24.146 --> 00:36:25.178
Is any of this true?

00:36:25.209 --> 00:36:26.461
No. Don't listen to them.

00:36:26.487 --> 00:36:27.791
They're liars, and they're dangerous.

00:36:27.947 --> 00:36:29.574
Something tried to drown me.

00:36:30.122 --> 00:36:31.405
Chris died on that lake.

00:36:31.436 --> 00:36:32.578
Dad, look at me.

00:36:35.894 --> 00:36:36.566
Tell me you

00:36:36.629 --> 00:36:38.162
You didn't kill anyone.

00:36:48.050 --> 00:36:49.161
Oh, my god.

00:36:53.213 --> 00:36:54.709
Billy and I were at the lake.

00:36:57.791 --> 00:37:00.420
Peter was the smallest
one. We always bullied him,

00:37:00.952 --> 00:37:02.062
But this time...

00:37:03.319 --> 00:37:04.414
It got rough.

00:37:09.343 --> 00:37:10.985
We were holding his
head under the water.

00:37:11.882 --> 00:37:13.134
We didn't mean to,

00:37:13.963 --> 00:37:15.653
But we held him under too long,

00:37:15.778 --> 00:37:16.983
And he drowned.

00:37:23.975 --> 00:37:25.289
We let the body go,

00:37:26.009 --> 00:37:27.073
And it sank.

00:37:34.146 --> 00:37:35.382
Oh, Andrea.

00:37:38.485 --> 00:37:39.659
We were kids.

00:37:40.159 --> 00:37:41.051
We were so scared.

00:37:41.082 --> 00:37:42.099
It was a mistake,

00:37:42.115 --> 00:37:42.970
But, Andrea,

00:37:43.262 --> 00:37:45.671
To say that I have anything
to do with these drownings,

00:37:45.702 --> 00:37:46.829
With Chris,

00:37:47.251 --> 00:37:48.894
Because of some ghost

00:37:49.176 --> 00:37:50.725
It's not rational.

00:37:51.746 --> 00:37:53.013
All right, listen to me,

00:37:53.514 --> 00:37:54.468
All of you.

00:37:55.141 --> 00:37:56.643
We need to get you away from this lake

00:37:56.737 --> 00:37:58.379
As far as we can right now.

00:38:02.304 --> 00:38:02.882
Lucas!

00:38:06.705 --> 00:38:08.754
Come play with me.

00:38:09.662 --> 00:38:10.444
Lucas!

00:38:10.636 --> 00:38:13.327
Lucas! Stay where you are!

00:38:32.315 --> 00:38:33.410
Oh, my god!

00:38:36.883 --> 00:38:38.072
Andrea, stay there.

00:38:38.213 --> 00:38:39.293
No, Lucas!

00:38:39.345 --> 00:38:40.643
We'll get him. Stay on the dock.

00:38:46.929 --> 00:38:47.904
Lucas?

00:38:50.622 --> 00:38:51.420
Sam?

00:38:53.313 --> 00:38:54.862
Lucas, where are you?

00:38:59.138 --> 00:38:59.764
Peter,

00:38:59.936 --> 00:39:00.906
If you can hear me,

00:39:02.068 --> 00:39:03.006
Please, Peter,

00:39:03.038 --> 00:39:03.789
I'm sorry.

00:39:05.275 --> 00:39:06.104
I'm so... Dad, no!

00:39:06.151 --> 00:39:07.215
I'm so sorry.

00:39:07.716 --> 00:39:08.279
Peter.

00:39:08.514 --> 00:39:09.202
Lucas

00:39:09.499 --> 00:39:11.658
He's j... he's just a little boy.

00:39:12.367 --> 00:39:14.448
Please, it's not his fault. It's mine.

00:39:14.589 --> 00:39:15.762
Please take me!

00:39:16.763 --> 00:39:17.311
Jake,

00:39:17.373 --> 00:39:17.733
No!

00:39:19.032 --> 00:39:20.487
Listen, let it be over!

00:39:22.748 --> 00:39:23.436
Dad

00:39:24.268 --> 00:39:25.099
Daddy!

00:39:27.632 --> 00:39:28.492
No

00:39:38.486 --> 00:39:39.346
No...

00:40:19.737 --> 00:40:20.473
Look,

00:40:21.302 --> 00:40:22.679
We're not gonna save everybody.

00:40:25.312 --> 00:40:25.969
I know.

00:40:26.751 --> 00:40:27.502
Sam,

00:40:27.878 --> 00:40:28.566
Dean.

00:40:28.707 --> 00:40:29.473
Hey.

00:40:31.194 --> 00:40:32.352
We're glad we caught you.

00:40:32.790 --> 00:40:33.682
We just, um,

00:40:34.875 --> 00:40:36.377
We made you lunch for the road.

00:40:37.159 --> 00:40:39.897
Lucas insisted on making
the sandwiches himself.

00:40:41.372 --> 00:40:42.421
Can I give it to them now?

00:40:44.345 --> 00:40:44.955
Of course.

00:40:46.174 --> 00:40:47.989
Come on, Lucas, let's
load this in the car.

00:40:54.611 --> 00:40:55.549
How you holding up?

00:40:57.990 --> 00:41:00.916
It's just gonna take a long time to
sort through everything, you know?

00:41:04.863 --> 00:41:06.459
Andrea, I'm sorry.

00:41:08.054 --> 00:41:09.259
You saved my son.

00:41:11.043 --> 00:41:12.779
I can't ask for more than that.

00:41:16.454 --> 00:41:17.315
Dad loved me.

00:41:18.441 --> 00:41:19.693
He loved Lucas.

00:41:20.679 --> 00:41:21.680
No matter what he did,

00:41:21.701 --> 00:41:22.822
I just have to...

00:41:24.579 --> 00:41:25.628
Hold on to that.

00:41:31.825 --> 00:41:32.643
All right,

00:41:32.806 --> 00:41:34.277
If you're gonna be talking now,

00:41:34.572 --> 00:41:37.580
This is a very important phrase, so
I want you to repeat it one more time.

00:41:37.776 --> 00:41:38.730
Zeppelin rules!

00:41:38.734 --> 00:41:40.140
That's right. Up high.

00:41:43.826 --> 00:41:45.786
Take care of your mom, okay?

00:41:53.731 --> 00:41:55.268
Thank you.

00:42:00.444 --> 00:42:01.719
Sam, move your ass.

00:42:02.112 --> 00:42:04.172
We're gonna run out of
daylight before we hit the road.



